.el .ds Aq '
.TH forgehub 1  "forgehub 0.1.6" 
.SH NAME
forgehub \- ForgeHub \- a cloud home for shell command snippets
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBforgehub\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-offline\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Save shell command snippets once, run them anywhere with `fg <name>`. Local commands work fully offline; cloud commands (login, push, pull, fork) sync with your ForgeHub server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print machine\-readable JSON instead of human output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts (never bypasses hash\-change or third\-party trust prompts; see spec\-cli §7)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose request logging to stderr (method, status, timing; tokens are never printed)
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Offline mode: cloud commands fail fast with an offline message; local commands and `run \-\-offline` still work
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Colour output: `auto` colours only on a capable terminal and honours `NO_COLOR`; `never` is always plain. Default: the `color` key from `fg config`, else `auto`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Colour when stdout is a terminal, `NO_COLOR` is unset and `TERM` is not `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Colour even when piped (still honours nothing else)
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never colour
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
forgehub\-init(1)
Create the `ForgeHub` home and config
.TP
forgehub\-record(1)
Record a shell session as a snippet
.TP
forgehub\-run(1)
Run a snippet by name
.TP
forgehub\-list(1)
List local snippets
.TP
forgehub\-show(1)
Show a snippet (card + numbered commands)
.TP
forgehub\-search(1)
Search local snippets (name, description, tags, commands)
.TP
forgehub\-find(1)
Fuzzy\-find snippets by name (local library + cached cloud names), ranked
.TP
forgehub\-tag(1)
Add or remove tags: fg tag <name> add|remove <tag>…
.TP
forgehub\-rename(1)
Rename a local snippet
.TP
forgehub\-delete(1)
Delete a local snippet
.TP
forgehub\-new(1)
Create a snippet from a template and open it in $EDITOR; validation errors loop back into the editor
.TP
forgehub\-lint(1)
Lint a snippet (danger lints + secret scan) without running anything. Exit 0 clean, 1 warnings, 2 blocking
.TP
forgehub\-edit(1)
Edit a snippet in $EDITOR; invalid edits are rolled back. An `owner/name` reference edits your cloud snippet and pushes the result as a new version after confirmation
.TP
forgehub\-parameterize(1)
Turn repeated literals into variables
.TP
forgehub\-clone(1)
Duplicate a local snippet under a new name
.TP
forgehub\-import(1)
Import snippet file(s) (`ForgeHub` or Forgenesis format)
.TP
forgehub\-export(1)
Export a snippet as YAML (to stdout or a file)
.TP
forgehub\-analyze(1)
Mine shell history for repeated command sequences
.TP
forgehub\-stats(1)
Show run statistics from history.db
.TP
forgehub\-backup(1)
Write a backup archive (default: backups/forgehub\-backup\-<timestamp>.tar)
.TP
forgehub\-restore(1)
Restore snippets from a backup archive
.TP
forgehub\-login(1)
Log in to a `ForgeHub` server (device\-code flow in the browser)
.TP
forgehub\-logout(1)
Log out: delete the stored credential for a registry
.TP
forgehub\-whoami(1)
Show the current login (username, registry, token, scopes)
.TP
forgehub\-push(1)
Push a local snippet to the cloud (create or new version)
.TP
forgehub\-pull(1)
Pull a cloud snippet into the local library
.TP
forgehub\-status(1)
Compare local snippets with the cloud (ahead/behind/diverged)
.TP
forgehub\-diff(1)
Unified diff of a local snippet against the cloud latest
.TP
forgehub\-history(1)
Show a cloud snippet\*(Aqs version history (versions are immutable; local\-only snippets have none)
.TP
forgehub\-rollback(1)
Roll a snippet back: publish an old version\*(Aqs content as a NEW version (history is never rewritten)
.TP
forgehub\-fork(1)
Fork someone\*(Aqs snippet into your account (server\-side)
.TP
forgehub\-remote(1)
Inspect and manage your cloud snippets
.TP
forgehub\-trust(1)
Manage execution trust for cloud snippets (Step 13): `trust list`, `trust revoke <owner/name>`, or approve an exact snippet directly: `trust <owner/name@hash>`
.TP
forgehub\-doctor(1)
Check the environment and library health
.TP
forgehub\-alias(1)
Manage the `fg` shell alias (install|uninstall|show)
.TP
forgehub\-completions(1)
Print shell completions (dynamic: local snippet names included)
.TP
forgehub\-ui(1)
Browse snippets in a terminal UI (Local · Mine · Explore)
.TP
forgehub\-cache(1)
Inspect and manage the cloud run cache
.TP
forgehub\-collection(1)
Manage snippet collections: ordered runbooks you can share and run end to end with `fg run <collection>`
.TP
forgehub\-config(1)
Read and write the local configuration (registry, colour, shell, default visibility, cache size). No secrets: tokens stay in the credential store
.TP
forgehub\-update(1)
Check whether a newer `ForgeHub` is available (never downloads or replaces anything)
.TP
forgehub\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Concepts: fg help <topic> \- alias, trust, hash\-pinning, yes, offline
.SH VERSION
v0.1.6 (6df66541c1f3, built 2026\-11\-20)
